// Śrī Lalitā Triśatī (ककाररूपा कल्याणी कल्याणगुणशालिनी …), the three hundred names of Lalitā
// Tripurasundarī taught by Hayagrīva to Agastya in the Lalitopākhyāna of the Brahmāṇḍa Purāṇa:
// the stotra in 59 verses, then the same names as a namāvalī.
// Collated Nov 2026; not yet checked line by line against a printed edition.
//
// Sources:
//   A. stotranidhi.com, "Śrī Lalitā Triśatī Stotram" (Devanagari; from the printed "Prabhāta Stotranidhi"):
//      the 59 verses, base text; and "Śrī Lalitā Triśatī Nāmāvalī" (Devanagari), the 300 names in the dative.
//   B. stotrasamhita/stotra-sangrahah (GitHub), stotras/big/LalitaTrishati.tex: the stotra.
//   C. sa.wikisource, "ललितात्रिशतीभाष्यम्" (Śaṅkarācārya's commentary, printed 1910), which quotes every
//      verse and every name; its digital text is noisy and was used only to confirm names and word order.
// Differences from A, resolved by B and C (and by sense):
//   v45 सकलाधिष्ठानरूपा, समानाधिकवर्जिता (B C, and the namāvalī) / सकालाधिष्ठान-…, समनाधिक- (A, misprints)
//   namāvalī 140 सर्वभूषणभूषितायै and 182 लतापूज्यायै (stotra, C) / -भुषितायै, लतापुज्यायै (A, misprints)
//   namāvalī 100 and 99: the stotra's "ह्रीं ह्रींशरीरिणी" is read as two names, ह्रीं and ह्रींशरीरिणी
//   ह्रींकार is written with anusvara throughout (B writes ह्रीङ्कार; A has anusvara with ZWJ)
// B agrees with A in all other words; it differs in word-joining (hyphens) only.
// NOT INCLUDED: the Pūrvapīṭhikā (Agastya-Hayagrīva dialogue, 28 verses) and the Uttarapīṭhikā (phalaśruti
// and the Śrīcakra passage, about 60 verses); also the viniyoga and nyāsa lines, because the witnesses
// disagree about the bīja/śakti/kīlaka (A: aiṃ bījam, sauḥ śaktiḥ, klīṃ kīlakam; B: aiṃ, klīṃ, sauḥ).
